    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are an employee of a faceless corporation named W.A.K.E.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dropped on an alien ocean world with one directive: Explore. Why? You don\u2019t know. You just follow orders, printed coldly from a terminal in your cabin.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore, Upgrade, and Uncover the Unknown</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Navigate a vast, procedurally generated world from the deck of your drone ship in this top-down exploration game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udee5\ufe0f <strong>15 Unique Ships</strong> \u2013 Each with distinct strengths, upgradeable stats, and abilities.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udf0d <strong>Endless Procedural Maps</strong> \u2013 No two expeditions are the same. Discover shifting biomes, colourful terrain and hidden buildings.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f <strong>Upgradeable Buildings</strong> \u2013 Find Research Stations to enhance ship capabilities and Harbor's to unlock more powerful vessels.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udd27 <strong>Persistent Progression</strong> \u2013 Earn Coins, Research Points, and rare Sub-nautical Data to continually improve your fleet and efficiency.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83c\udfaf <strong>Objective System</strong> \u2013 Complete your mapping assignments to progress to new planets, unlocking new ships and technologies</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udcc8 <strong>Highscores &amp; Endless Levels</strong> \u2013 Compete, improve, and push deeper into uncharted waters.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are not told the reasons. Only the results.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Follow the orders. Expand your fleet. Dive deeper</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >How far can your ship go?</p>",
